  "description": "A full VTD proof (SIGE spec 5.5A req 2, Fiat-Shamir cut-and-choose over LHTLP-locked Shamir shares) from a fixed seed. Seed derivation (src/core/vectors.ts): seededBytes(label, length) concatenates SHA-256 blocks sha256(seedDomain + '/' + label + u32be(counter)) for counter = 0, 1, 2, ..., truncated to length bytes; seededScalar(label, order) reduces seededBytes(label + '#' + attempt, 48) mod order, retrying attempt = 0..7 on a zero result; seededSquareUnit(label, n) squares seededScalar(label, n) mod n after checking it is coprime to n. lhtlpParams.p/q are the public Mersenne primes 2^127-1 and 2^521-1, chosen so k*Fr.ORDER^2 < n holds for k=3 with margin (unlike lhtlp.json's toy-scale demo, this modulus is sized for the real fold bound); lhtlpParams.g = seededSquareUnit(gSeed, n). secret = seededScalar(secretSeed, Fr.ORDER); nonce = seededBytes(nonceSeed, 32); each blinding = seededScalar(blindingSeeds[i], lhtlpParams.n). Polynomial coefficients derive from (secret, nonce) via HKDF-SHA256: info = utf8(\"sige-vtd/coefficient\") || nonce || u32be(j) || u32be(attempt), ikm = secret as big-endian bytes, salt is empty, output length 48 bytes, reduced mod Fr.ORDER and retried by incrementing attempt on a zero result. The proof's challenge derivation uses four further domain strings through the same dhash construction (SHA256(\"SIGE-DEMO/v1\" || u32be(len(domain)) || domain || u32be(len(part))+part for each part)): \"sige-vtd/index\" (the top challenge, over params/nonce/commitments/puzzles/profile), \"sige-vtd/index-expand\" (per-counter index draw), \"sige-vtd/weights\" (the batched-Feldman weight challenge, over the index challenge and the opened shares), \"sige-vtd/weights-expand\" (per-counter weight draw). commitments, puzzles and opened shares follow from the public library (commitPoly, shareAt, createPuzzle) plus the exported challenge/index-set derivation. verifyVtd must return null, solveVtd must return secret, coefficientsDeriveFromSecret must return null. soundnessBits and worstCaseSolves are pure functions of profile, included for convenience. Independently cross-checked: the HKDF coefficient derivation against node:crypto hkdfSync (both j=1 and j=2); soundnessBits against the hand-derived closed form -log2(C(n-b,o)/C(n,o)) = log2(2.5) for n=6,k=3,o=2,b=2.",
